Bootstrap: docker
From: earthquakesuc/workflow-bootstrap:latest

%files
    EMOD3D /EMOD3D

%post
    # CMAKE_C_FLAGS_DEBUG/CMAKE_Fortran_FLAGS_DEBUG are set explicitly because
    # the top-level CMakeLists.txt appends -O2 to CMAKE_{C,Fortran}_FLAGS
    # unconditionally. The per-config flags land last on the command line, so
    # these are what actually make the build unoptimised.
    cd /EMOD3D && \
      mkdir build && cd build && \
      cmake -DHF_TIME_WINDOW=off -DUSE_FFTW=on -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Debug \
            -DCMAKE_C_FLAGS="-march=x86-64 -mtune=generic -std=gnu89" \
            -DCMAKE_C_FLAGS_DEBUG="-O0 -g3 -fno-omit-frame-pointer" \
            -DCMAKE_Fortran_FLAGS_DEBUG="-O0 -g3 -fno-omit-frame-pointer" .. && \
      make -j $(nproc) genslip_v5.6.2 srf2stoch generic_slip2srf \
                      hb_high_binmod_v6.0.3 emod3d-mpi_v3.0.4 \
                      emod3d-mpi_v3.0.8 emod3d-mpi_v3.0.13

    cd /
    # Unlike runner.def, keep the sources alongside the binaries: the DWARF
    # records absolute /EMOD3D paths, so gdb resolves line numbers unaided.
    # Only the object files go.
    rm -rf /EMOD3D/build

%environment
    export RUSTUP_HOME=/sw/rust
    export CARGO_HOME=/sw/cargo
    export PATH="/sw/venv/bin:/EMOD3D/tools:/sw/cargo/bin:/sw/python/bin:$PATH"
    export VIRTUAL_ENV="/sw/venv"
    export LD_LIBRARY_PATH="/usr/local/lib:$LD_LIBRARY_PATH"

%labels
    Build_Type debug
    Debug_Flags -O0 -g3 -fno-omit-frame-pointer

%help
    Debug counterpart to runner.def. Every EMOD3D target is built unoptimised
    with full DWARF, and the source tree is retained under /EMOD3D so that
    gdb (already present in the base image) can step through it.

    In addition to the four tools runner.sif ships, this image also carries the
    LF solver, which runner.sif does not build at all:
        emod3d-mpi_v3.0.4  emod3d-mpi_v3.0.8  emod3d-mpi_v3.0.13

    Build (the %files source is relative to the CWD you launch the build from,
    so a directory named EMOD3D must sit there):
        git -C <emod3d-checkout> archive HEAD --prefix=EMOD3D/ | tar -x -C .
        apptainer build debug_runner.sif <path-to>/debug_runner.def

    The solver must be launched through mpirun/srun even for a single rank.
    Invoked directly it hangs in OpenMPI's singleton startup, which looks like
    an unrelated "Authorization required" message.

    Debug a solver run:
        apptainer exec debug_runner.sif \
            mpirun -n 1 gdb -ex run --args \
            emod3d-mpi_v3.0.13 -args "par=/path/to/e3d.par"
